Full prime-degree total-real-period/kernel-cokernel identity, the real
case classification and full-relative nonoptimal transfer: not checked.
Supporting Tate modules, isogeny invariance, modular forms, rational
cancellation, integral generation and p-adic valuations: not checked.
Unknown coverage is not evidence of absence. The precise published
period theorem and granted audited normalization supply the mathematical
inputs; no formal verification or universal software theorem is claimed.
